JavaScript has two methods of handling asynchronous code: callbacks and async/await. Callbacks are a function that executes a piece of code and then passes control back to another function. Async/await is a more readable and maintainable way of writing asynchronous code. It is a new JavaScript syntax for writing asynchronous code that uses the words 'await' and 'async'.

